    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Extension: From Minimum Finding to Quantum Sort\n",
        "\n",
        "Durr-Hoyer Minimum Finding can be used as the basic operation for a quantum sorting approach.\n",
        "\n",
        "After finding the minimum of the complete array, that element is placed in its correct position. The same minimum-finding procedure is then applied to the remaining unsorted elements.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "[7,2,9,4,1,6,8,3]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "can be processed through repeated minimum finding:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "1\\rightarrow2\\rightarrow3\\rightarrow4\\rightarrow6\\rightarrow7\\rightarrow8\\rightarrow9\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "giving the sorted array\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "[1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{Quantum Minimum Finding}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{Repeated Minimum Finding}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{Sorted Array}\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This shows how repeated application of Durr-Hoyer Minimum Finding can form the basis of a **quantum sorting approach**, without requiring a separate Quantum Sort implementation."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JVReeW79JKtx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def quantum_sort(arr):\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Make a copy so the original array is not modified\n",
        "    arr = arr.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    n = len(arr)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Repeatedly find the minimum of the unsorted portion\n",
        "    for i in range(n):\n",
        "\n",
        "        remaining = arr[i:]\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Apply quantum minimum finding\n",
        "        rel_index, rel_value = durr_hoyer_minimum(\n",
        "            remaining\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Convert relative index to actual index\n",
        "        actual_index = i + rel_index\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Place the minimum element at position i\n",
        "        arr[i], arr[actual_index] = (\n",
        "            arr[actual_index],\n",
        "            arr[i]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return arr"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VY95HJNNJskS"
      },
